  "id": "post-event-skysat-2026-08-31",
  "title": "Betrawati to Trishuli Bazaar (SkySat) — Post-event Imagery",
  "description": "High-resolution SkySat coverage of the lower corridor, acquired 09:25 UTC on 31 August 2026, five days after the flood. Two collects run south from around Betrawati to the Trishuli Bazaar (Bidur) area, taking in a river confluence and the largest settlement imaged anywhere in this catalog at sub-metre resolution. At roughly 0.64 m they resolve individual buildings, bridges and the braided channel. This is the first high-resolution coverage of the downstream reach — the 27 August SkySat and Pelican collects both sit upstream between 28.08 and 28.37 N. Planet reports 76% cloud and 12% clear, but as elsewhere in this catalog that understates usable ground: much of both frames is legible, and a broad pale sediment-filled channel is clearly traceable through the centre. A 42 degree sun elevation gives shorter shadows and more even illumination than the 27 August collects. The pre-event PlanetScope strip covers this same ground, so before/after comparison is possible here, though at 3.8 m against 0.64 m. 2 scenes; each Item carries the available visual, pansharpened, udm assets.",
